      "writtenOn": "2025-07-14T22:19:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about specifying a newer Xcode version for now and see if that works?\n\nSpecifying a newer version of macOS will ultimately require the data center that hosts the Macs to have machines with that OS version. We can check later, but machines with a different dimension may not be available.\n\nFor reference: third_party/depot_tools/recipes/recipe_modules/osx_sdk/api.py has the macOS to Xcode mapping.\n\nAlso, https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/embedder-dev/c/SiZ-erHY-G0 says macOS 12 is still supported, though that is for end users, not developers.",
      "parentUuid": "2511f1d4_d66638ae",
      "revId": "55f199c44c9da983d36ba445471e4efbd3e7eeff",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
